@broadcast "Coldwater A.M."
@category morning
@length 240
@type scripted

::actors
@actor npc_am_pace
@alias npc_am_pace BIJOU
@actor npc_am_dorn
@alias npc_am_dorn HAL
::endactors

::asset coldwater_am_logo

╔═══════════════════════════════════════╗
║                                       ║
║        C O L D W A T E R   A.M.       ║
║                                       ║
║     "You're up. Might as well be."    ║
║                                       ║
╚═══════════════════════════════════════╝

::endasset

::asset am_basin_beat_card

▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄
█   T H E   B A S I N   B E A T   █
█    stories from your street     █
▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀

::endasset

::scene COLD_OPEN

ROOM zone_studio_1782953094650

EVENT FADE_IN

MUSIC coldwater_am_theme
♪ Bright synthetic brass, the audio equivalent of a smile held too long. ♪
MUSIC_END

TITLE coldwater_am_logo

CAM 1 WIDE morning_couch

SHOT
Two hosts sit on a curved orange couch in front of a window that is not a window. Behind the glass, a looped sunrise plays. It is raining outside the building.
SHOT_END

ENTER npc_am_pace

BIJOU:
Good MORNING, Coldwater! It is six o'clock, it is four degrees, and you are ALIVE!

ENTER npc_am_dorn

HAL:
Statistically.

BIJOU:
Statistically alive! I'm Bijou Pace.

HAL:
Hal Dorn.

ACTION npc_am_dorn holds his mug with both hands like a man warming himself at a very small fire.

BIJOU:
And we have SUCH a show for you.

::scene BASIN_BEAT

CAM 2 MEDIUM two_shot

TITLE am_basin_beat_card

LOWER_THIRD
THE BASIN BEAT
STORIES FROM YOUR STREET
LOWER_THIRD_END

BIJOU:
First up — a heartwarming one. A Redline man has been reunited with his dog!

HAL:
He has been reunited with a dog.

BIJOU:
He has been reunited with A dog, and honestly? At this hour, that's a win.

ACTION npc_am_pace beams directly down the lens with the full force of a woman who has decided.

HAL:
The original dog remains outstanding.

BIJOU:
The original dog remains outstanding! Moving on!

NARRATOR:
Coldwater A.M. is brought to you by the people who would like you at work on time.

::scene KITCHEN

CAM 3 CLOSEUP hotplate

SHOT
A single induction ring on a laminate counter. Bijou stands behind it holding an unlabelled grey tube. Hal has not moved from the couch.
SHOT_END

BIJOU:
Now — breakfast! Because the most important meal of the day is the one you can afford.

BIJOU:
Take your standard ration paste. Squeeze it into a pan. And here's the trick — heat.

ACTION npc_am_pace squeezes the tube into the pan. The sound is upsetting.

HAL:
That's the trick.

BIJOU:
That's the WHOLE trick, Hal. Two minutes, and it goes from grey to a sort of warmer grey.

HAL:
My father used to do that.

ACTION npc_am_dorn looks at the middle distance for slightly longer than the format allows.

BIJOU:
Lovely! And if you've got a little sweetener, stir it through at the end and you have got yourself a TREAT.

::scene TRAFFIC

CAM 1 WIDE morning_couch

LOWER_THIRD
YOUR MORNING RUN-IN
CURFEW LIFTS 06:30 · SOUTH GATE DELAYS
LOWER_THIRD_END

HAL:
Curfew lifts at half six. South Gate is running long — they're searching everybody again.

HAL:
If you're heading in from the wastes, leave an hour. If you're carrying anything you'd rather not explain, leave it.

BIJOU:
Ha ha! Hal!

HAL:
I'm saying leave it at home. I'm saying that as a service.

BIJOU:
Haulage is slow on the Haul Road, the North Locks are frozen again, and the Basin is BEAUTIFUL this morning if you don't look directly at it.

::scene SIGNOFF

CAM 2 MEDIUM two_shot

BIJOU:
That's us! Back tomorrow, same couch, same sunrise.

HAL:
Same sunrise.

ACTION npc_am_dorn glances at the window that is not a window.

BIJOU:
Go and have a WONDERFUL day, Coldwater. You've earned it. Probably.

TICKER
COLDWATER A.M. · Curfew lifts 06:30 · South Gate: extended searches, allow one hour · North Locks closed to foot traffic · Ration distribution at Meltwater Row from 07:00, bring documentation · Overnight vat intake was within normal range · The sunrise depicted is a composite and does not reflect current conditions
TICKER_END

MUSIC coldwater_am_theme
♪ The bright brass returns, one semitone flatter than it started. ♪
MUSIC_END

CREDITS 5
COLDWATER A.M.
Presented by Bijou Pace and Hal Dorn.
Hal Dorn appears by arrangement with his contract.
END_CREDITS

EVENT FADE_OUT

END
